From de568b3ffd3619ceccc277efaf920e0df2e8a2bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Miloslav=20Mac=C5=AFrek?= <macurek.m@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 13:49:48 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Phase 4.1: instrument the oracle with the shared counter
 set

Implements the oracle side of analysis/phase4_counter_spec.md (on dev) so 4.2
can compare Rarog against this revision counter-for-counter instead of choosing
the first cluster by intuition.

Adds rarog_diag.{h,cpp}: an X-macro counter table mirroring Rarog's declare!
pattern, emitting the identical `info string diag <name> <value>` shape, so a
differential run is a plain textual join on the name. Instruments search.cpp
and movepick.cpp at the sites the spec names, by upstream step number.

Gated on RAROG_DIAG, off by default. Verified rather than assumed:

  diag OFF   bench 16 1 7 = 136,903 nodes, bestmove e7e3 -- identical to the
             frozen dist binary at 75d0d43, and zero diag lines emitted
  diag ON    bench 16 1 7 = 136,903 nodes -- instrumentation does not perturb
             the tree

Three real defects were caught by verifying instead of shipping:

1. The root_best_changes insert landed inside an unbraced `if`, making
   ++bestMoveChanges unconditional -- in BOTH builds, since DIAG_COUNT expands
   to ((void)0) when the flag is off. That would have silently changed the
   frozen engine's time management. Braced, and every other insertion audited
   for the same shape.
2. probcut_cut exceeded probcut_attempt, because the TT-served ProbCut
   shortcut returns without running a search. A rate above 1 discredits a
   diagnostic, so the shortcut now counts as both. Re-verified: cut <= attempt
   in all 44 bench positions.
3. CXXFLAGS += -DRAROG_DIAG was initially placed before the Makefile's own
   CXXFLAGS line and would have been dropped; moved after it.

Built-in cross-checks that now pass and should keep passing: best_rank_1 equals
cutoff_first_move exactly (1433/1433 at depth 9), the four rank buckets sum to
cutoff_quiet + cutoff_capture (1726), main_tt_probes equals nodes, and
main_store_lower equals the cutoff total. If any of these separates, the
instrumentation is wrong, not the engine.

Notes for 4.2, from the first reading:

- singular_extend_two and singular_negative_extension are structurally ABSENT
  here -- both mechanisms postdate this revision. They read 0 always and must
  not be read as "the oracle extends less"; Rarog has them and the reference
  does not.
- nmp_verify_* only fires at depth >= 13, so short-depth suites read 0. Not a
  gap.
- prune_shadow_moves excludes quiets the picker withheld under LMP, because
  the threshold is enforced in movepick rather than by a `continue`. LMP's
  overlap with futility/SEE is therefore only observable at the boundary move.
- The suite must drive `bench`, not piped `go ... quit`: a piped quit is read
  before the search starts and aborts it, which is why a naive `go depth 10`
  returns bestmove a2a3 on the frozen binary too.

Build: make build ARCH=x86-64-bmi2 COMP=mingw diag=yes
This artifact is diagnostic only. It never plays a rating game and never
replaces the frozen 75d0d43 tournament binary.

Note: /hybrid/ is listed in .git/info/exclude, so the new files needed
`git add -f`. Anything added here later needs the same, or it is silently lost.
