From 49ab5b03c55815d05a36f2903e49a834d41c7972 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Miloslav=20Mac=C5=AFrek?= <macurek.m@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 14:53:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] 4.7b correction: lmp_prune was never comparable; rename
 to lmp_nodes

My own 4.1 instrumentation had the RAR-S25 denominator bug in it.

The oracle's counter fires at most ONCE per node -- reaching the QUIET stage
with skipQuiets set advances past it -- so it counts NODES whose quiets were
suppressed. Rarog's lmp_prune fires per skipped MOVE, inside the move loop.

RAR-S55 reported lmp_prune at 13.35x normalised and the 4.3 map made it the
second-ranked lead for cluster 4.7. That number is comparing moves-skipped
against nodes-that-skipped. It is an artifact.

Renamed to lmp_nodes on the oracle side, which is what it measures. Rarog gets
a matching per-node counter next; its per-move lmp_prune stays as a Rarog-only
reading rather than being redefined, since it is genuinely informative about
volume -- just not against this.

Verified pure rename: bench 16 1 7 still 136,903 nodes.

Caught while designing 4.7b on the strength of that 13.35x, which is the
cheapest possible place to catch it -- one step before it would have justified
a code change and a game budget.
---
