From 2682f64afe4137c2f89d332b4e2008d51aeaa9c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Miloslav=20Mac=C5=AFrek?= <macurek.m@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 14:18:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] 4.7c prep: probcut_attempt was per MOVE against Rarog's
 per NODE

Same denominator class as 4.7b, one lead later, found by auditing the counter
before designing against it rather than after.

The oracle's probcut_attempt fires inside the MovePicker loop -- once per move
actually searched, up to 2 + 2*cutNode at a node. Rarog's fires once per NODE
entering the ProbCut block, before capture generation, so nodes with no
eligible capture still count an attempt. RAR-S55's "conversion 22.7% against
91.2%" divides cuts-per-node by cuts-per-move-tried. It is a category error,
and unlike 4.7b the direction of the correction was not predictable in advance,
because the oracle's nodes-entered count did not exist.

Now it does. Three changes, oracle side only:

  probcut_nodes      NEW. Per node passing the entry gate, counted before the
                     TT shortcut and before the MovePicker, so it includes
                     nodes where the picker yields nothing and no search ever
                     starts. This is what Rarog's per-node counter compares to.
  probcut_tt_served  NEW. The TT-served shortcut returns probcutBeta without
                     running any search. 4.1 made it count as probcut_attempt
                     so the rate would not read above 1; that hid it. It is a
                     cutoff but not an attempt, so it now has its own counter.
                     Rarog has no TT-served ProbCut path, so this population
                     must be visible in order to be subtracted.
  probcut_attempt    Unchanged in position and meaning -- per move searched,
                     which is exactly what the spec text says. It is Rarog's
                     counter that does not match the spec, so the rename falls
                     on the Rarog side, mirroring the 4.7b treatment.

Verified rather than assumed, both directions:

  diag=yes   bench 16 1 7 = 136,903 nodes -- instrumentation does not perturb
             the tree, same fingerprint 4.1 established
  diag=no    bench 16 1 7 = 136,903 nodes, zero diag lines emitted -- an
             ordinary build of this branch is still the frozen oracle

All three inserts sit inside existing braces; audited against 4.1's defect 1,
where an insert landed in an unbraced if and silently changed the frozen
engine's time management in BOTH builds.

First reading, from the 47 bench positions at depth 7 -- a fingerprint check,
NOT the measurement, which is the 4.2 suite at depth 8:

  probcut_nodes      1,623     entered the block
  probcut_tt_served    939     57.9% of entries returned from the TT, unsearched
  probcut_attempt      218     moves actually searched, across 684 non-TT nodes
  probcut_cut        1,118     of which 939 are the TT path

So the oracle's 91.2% was overwhelmingly the TT shortcut. Netting it out gives
179 search-produced cuts from 684 nodes that reached the picker: 26.2% per
node, against Rarog's 22.7%. Different suite and depth, so those two numbers
are not yet a finding -- but the gap that ranked ProbCut second in the 4.3 map
is not visible in this reading, and 68% of the nodes reaching the oracle's
picker search nothing at all, which is the SEE threshold doing the work the
conversion rate was being credited for.

Consequence for the Rarog side: tools/diag/phase4_differential.py:79 enforces
probcut_cut <= probcut_attempt, which this commit can now break on the oracle,
by design. It must become probcut_cut <= probcut_nodes, the invariant that
holds on both engines. That file and analysis/phase4_counter_spec.md are on
dev and change in the next commit.
---
 hybrid/stockfish/src/rarog_diag.h |  3 ++-
 hybrid/stockfish/src/search.cpp   | 18 +++++++++++++++---
 2 files changed, 17 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/hybrid/stockfish/src/rarog_diag.h b/hybrid/stockfish/src/rarog_diag.h
index acdd813..3a15300 100644
--- a/hybrid/stockfish/src/rarog_diag.h
+++ b/hybrid/stockfish/src/rarog_diag.h
@@ -43,7 +43,8 @@
         X(razor_drop) X(rfp_cut) \
         X(nmp_attempt) X(nmp_cut) \
         X(nmp_verify_attempt) X(nmp_verify_pass) X(nmp_verify_fail) \
-        X(probcut_attempt) X(probcut_cut) \
+        X(probcut_nodes) X(probcut_attempt) X(probcut_cut) \
+        X(probcut_tt_served) \
         X(lmp_nodes) X(quiet_futility_prune) X(see_prune) \
         /* 3b — prune recall and overlap */ \
         X(prune_shadow_moves) X(prune_shadow_lmp) X(prune_shadow_futility) \
diff --git a/hybrid/stockfish/src/search.cpp b/hybrid/stockfish/src/search.cpp
index 8ae173f..563425b 100644
--- a/hybrid/stockfish/src/search.cpp
+++ b/hybrid/stockfish/src/search.cpp
